  "term": "reflex sympathetic dystrophy",
  "definition": "Reflex sympathetic dystrophy is a syndrome in which an arm or leg develops severe burning pain along with changes in sweating, blood flow, and bone and skin nutrition, without a clearly identified specific nerve injury. It often follows trauma, and the affected area may become red and unusually sensitive to touch.",
